# Parent commit on quota (Cursor only)

**Host:** Cursor IDE / Cursor CLI only. Do **not** apply this under Claude Code —
Claude keeps the hard rule that the parent never runs `git commit`.

Default remains: spawn **`committer`** or run **`/land`** (see `agent-routing`).
`worker` still must not commit.

## Exception

When the user asked to **commit** (or `/land` needs the commit step) and spawning
**`committer`** fails because of rate-limit / quota / plan-usage (including after
the one `auto` retry from `subagent-model-fallback`):

1. Briefly note that `committer` is unavailable due to quota.
2. **Parent may** stage + `git commit` itself, following the usual git safety
   protocol (status/diff/log, HEREDOC message, no force-push, no amend unless
   the normal amend rules allow it, no secrets).
3. If the user also asked to **push**, parent may push after that commit (still
   no force-push to main/master unless they explicitly requested force).

## Still forbidden

- Parent commit when `committer` *can* spawn successfully — always prefer the pin.
- Parent commit for ordinary task failures (bad prompt, tool errors) — only for
  model/quota unavailability after the documented retry.
- Impersonating `committer`’s judgment when the user did **not** ask to commit;
  do not opportunistically commit.
- Changing Claude Code / shared `AGENT-ROUTING` protocol behavior via this rule.
